{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he shall sense.</b> Sometimes the perception of the ear misleads, so that it hears though there is no sound, and the eye too misleads, so that it sees a stationary object as moving. Only the perception of smell does not mislead. And he shall sense — as if he smells the matter by the fear of HaShem that he possesses. He shall not judge by what his eyes see, nor by what he hears, for the testimony of witnesses may be false." "And these reproofs and judgments are like the procedure of kingship."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:21.476629056Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}